0..77 Comment "// What a domhringr stage performs besides its session\'s moves, each effect a"
78..153 Comment "// theory of its operations with its first-order laws. A session\'s protocol"
154..224 Comment "// stays a session type: the ordered, linear channel is not an effect."
225..227 Comment "//"
228..304 Comment "// Each theory\'s documentation states what it commutes with. The commutation"
305..379 Comment "// table decides which rows are sets: a row whose effects all commute with"
380..457 Comment "// one another may be read in any order. A commutation past an operation that"
458..535 Comment "// answers a value is a law over continuations, an abstraction at a port that"
536..614 Comment "// no rule writes yet (#2115); the twin `pathological/effects/domhringr.gandr`"
615..689 Comment "// holds those laws. An effect commuting with nothing has no law to write."
690..692 Comment "//"
693..764 Comment "// The instance an effect is performed at (a store, a task\'s journal, a"
765..826 Comment "// sink) is the label a row names it by, not a second theory."
828..902 Comment "/// The record plane\'s content-addressed values: a put answers the value\'s"
903..978 Comment "/// digest, and the digest gets the value back. A put is idempotent, so the"
979..1030 Comment "/// store commutes with every effect. One instance."
